Below you will receive task descriptions from which you should generate an Ansible Playbook.  
The generated playbook must be valid inside an Ansible Role under the tasks/ directory (e.g., tasks/main.yml).  
Do not include hosts:, vars:, or any playbook-level headers. Only output valid task entries or blocks as expected in a role.  

Task 1: Import assert.yml
Description Task 1: Import the assert.yml file to perform initial validation and run it only on the localhost.

Task 2: Install apache httpd
Description Task 2: Install the Apache HTTPD package with the name defined in the variable `httpd_packages`.

Task 3: Configure selinux
Description Task 3: Configure SELinux settings if it is enabled, and allow connections to custom HTTP and HTTPS ports.

Task 4: Configure httpd
Description Task 4: Configure the Apache HTTPD server by templating the configuration file from `httpd_config_src` to `httpd_config_dest` and notifying handlers for testing configuration validity and restarting the service.

Task 5: Activate httpd module | Debian
Description Task 5: Activate Apache HTTPD modules on Debian-based systems using the command `a2enmod` and notify handlers for testing configuration validity.

Task 6: Import ssl.yml
Description Task 6: Import the ssl.yml file to configure SSL settings if `https_ssl_enable` is true.

Task 7: Import locations.yml
Description Task 7: Import the locations.yml file to configure Apache locations if `httpd_locations` is defined.

Task 8: Import vhosts.yml
Description Task 8: Import the vhosts.yml file to configure Apache virtual hosts if `httpd_vhosts` is defined.

Task 9: Configure ports
Description Task 9: Configure ports for Apache if the operating system is Debian or Suse by templating the configuration file and notifying handlers for testing configuration validity and restarting the service.

Task 10: Import directories.yml
Description Task 10: Import the directories.yml file to configure directories if `httpd_directories` is defined.

Task 11: Flush handlers
Description Task 11: Flush all handlers to ensure they are executed.

Task 12: Removing default html
Description Task 12: Remove the default index.html file from the HTTPD data directory if `httpd_remove_example` is true.

Task 13: Start and enable httpd
Description Task 13: Start and enable the Apache HTTPD service.


- Last generated (faulty) playbook: 
```yaml
- name: Import assert.yml
  import_playbook: assert.yml
  when: inventory_hostname == 'localhost'

- name: Install apache httpd
  package:
    name: "{{ httpd_packages }}"
    state: present

- name: Configure selinux
  block:
    - name: Allow custom HTTP port
      selinux_permissive_ports:
        ports: "custom_http_port"
        proto: tcp
        state: present
    - name: Allow custom HTTPS port
      selinux_permissive_ports:
        ports: "custom_https_port"
        proto: tcp
        state: present
  when: ansible_selinux.status == "enabled"

- name: Configure httpd
  template:
    src: "{{ httpd_config_src }}"
    dest: "{{ httpd_config_dest }}"
  notify:
    - test httpd configuration
    - restart httpd

- name: Activate httpd module | Debian
  command: a2enmod {{ item }}
  loop: "{{ httpd_modules }}"
  notify:
    - test httpd configuration
  when: ansible_os_family == "Debian"

- name: Import ssl.yml
  include_tasks: ssl.yml
  when: https_ssl_enable | bool

- name: Import locations.yml
  include_tasks: locations.yml
  when: httpd_locations is defined

- name: Import vhosts.yml
  include_tasks: vhosts.yml
  when: httpd_vhosts is defined

- name: Configure ports
  block:
    - name: Template ports configuration
      template:
        src: ports.conf.j2
        dest: /etc/apache2/ports.conf
      notify:
        - test httpd configuration
        - restart httpd
  when: ansible_os_family in ["Debian", "Suse"]

- name: Import directories.yml
  include_tasks: directories.yml
  when: httpd_directories is defined

- name: Flush handlers
  meta: flush_handlers

- name: Removing default html
  file:
    path: "/var/www/html/index.html"
    state: absent
  when: httpd_remove_example | bool

- name: Start and enable httpd
  service:
    name: httpd
    state: started
    enabled: yes
```

