```yaml
- name: Import assert.yml
  include_tasks:
    file: assert.yml
  when: ansible_play_hosts_all is defined

- name: Install required software
  apt:
    name: "{{ item }}"
    state: present
  loop: "{{ users_requirements | default([]) }}"
  when: users_requirements is defined and users_requirements | length > 0

- name: Loop over users_groups
  include_tasks:
    file: group.yml
  loop: "{{ users_groups | default([]) }}"
  when: users_groups is defined

- name: Ensure the /etc/sudoers.d directory is included
  lineinfile:
    path: /etc/sudoers
    line: 'Include /etc/sudoers.d/*'
    validate: visudo -cf %s
  when: users_sudo_includedir is defined and users_sudo_includedir | bool

- name: Loop over users
  include_tasks:
    file: user.yml
  loop: "{{ users | default([]) }}"
  when: users is defined

- name: Manage cron permission
  template:
    src: cron.allow.j2
    dest: /etc/cron.allow
  when: users_cron_allow is defined and users_cron_allow | bool

- name: Check existence of /etc/cron.allow
  file:
    path: /etc/cron.allow
    state: absent
  when: users_cron_allow is defined and not users_cron_allow | bool
```

This corrected playbook addresses the following issues:

1. Removed the `hosts: localhost` line, as it was causing a conflict with the `include_tasks` action.
2. Corrected the `include_tasks` syntax to use `file` instead of just specifying the file name directly. This is necessary for compatibility with newer Ansible versions.
3. Ensured all tasks are within a task list (block) context by using the `when` condition to apply to all tasks, which implicitly creates a block. This resolves the `block` property requirement.


